<title>PHILIPPINES: Ayala Land says 1996 net 4.0 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Ayala Land says 1996 net 4.0 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ayala Land Inc said on Friday its consolidated net income rose by 29 percent to four billion pesos in 1996.  </p>
<p>The country's premier real estate developer said in a statement the growth in its bottom line earnings last year was due to strong property sales and increased rental income from shopping centres, office buildings, hotels and other land sites.</p>
<p>&quot;Brisk land sales were experienced in Ayala Southvale residential lots, Laguna Technopark industrial lots and Madrigal Business Park commercial lots,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
</text>
